data/

# Raw Canvas captures. These contain third-party personal data (other students'
# names and emails in discussion topics and submission comments). They are
# redacted on write, but they never belong in version control. Enforced by
# .githooks/pre-commit -- see SPEC.md section 15 and DECISIONS.md D-11.
var/

# Local diagnostic output and the seed file. All three contain real module
# codes, real Canvas course ids, and my canvas_user_id. This repository is
# public (DECISIONS.md D-10), so none of them may be committed -- not even
# "just this once", because git history is not retractable.
#
# To share one of these safely, redact it and promote it to test/fixtures/
# under the policy in test/fixtures/README.md.
probe-*.txt
probe-*.log
discover-*.txt
discover-*.log
courses.seed.json

# The mirror's mapping (DECISIONS.md D-58): real term and module folder names.
# The committed mirror.config.example.json shows the shape with invented values.
mirror.config.json
